hud/statussources.mjs says where each state comes from. A caravan's
arrival is the S1 data the page already reads: on the road past its arrival
turn with no settlement read it is "not verified" (under the row that says
到着済み（決着待ち）), and a settlement read with its send read too compares
CARAVAN_SENT's cargo with CARAVAN_SETTLED's (partial or full, no cause
named). 04's cancel of a caravan, 05's costs of a village and 05's switch
back to manual play come from sources their owners register; with none
registered the S1 village card is as it was. Needs 0003 and 0004.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
